  "definitions": {
    "revenue": "Change in weighted government balance: reform gov_balance minus baseline gov_balance. Positive is a government gain. Includes tax and spending interactions; not income tax alone.",
    "decile_ranking": "Recomputed from the baseline for each reported year. Deciles of person-weighted equivalised HBAI household net income before housing costs; negative ranking income is reset to zero and equal-income households share a rank.",
    "decile_mean": "Weighted mean annual unequivalised household_net_income change among all households in the baseline decile, including unaffected households; household-weighted, not per person and not the mean among affected households.",
    "relative_change": "Sum of weighted household income change divided by sum of weighted baseline household income within that year's baseline decile, times100; not the mean of individual percentage changes.",
    "reach": "Share of people in households whose absolute change in household_net_income divided by max(baseline household_net_income,GBP1) exceeds0.0001 (0.01%). Numerator and denominator are weighted household size, restricted to baseline household_income_decile>=1. Changes in either direction count.",
    "gini_change": "(Reformed Gini minus baseline Gini)/baseline Gini, a relative fraction, using equivalised household_net_income with person weights. This is not a percentage-point change in the Gini coefficient."
  },
